then when you run it

00:34:11.640 --> 00:34:13.640
on the whole application

00:34:13.640 --> 00:34:15.640
we call this regression testing

00:34:15.640 --> 00:34:17.640
the simple foundation of regression testing

00:34:17.640 --> 00:34:19.640
is that if your version

00:34:19.640 --> 00:34:21.640
one of the software is running

00:34:21.640 --> 00:34:23.640
now you have made version two

00:34:23.640 --> 00:34:25.640
of the same software

00:34:25.640 --> 00:34:27.640
so how do you know version two

00:34:27.640 --> 00:34:29.640
is objectively not

00:34:29.640 --> 00:34:31.640
worse than version one

00:34:31.640 --> 00:34:33.640
is my application worse

00:34:33.639 --> 00:34:35.639
how do I test if it is not

00:34:35.639 --> 00:34:37.639
better than version one

00:34:37.639 --> 00:34:39.639
this is the answer you get in regression testing

00:34:39.639 --> 00:34:41.639
so there is nothing special in regression testing

00:34:41.639 --> 00:34:43.639
basically the eval suite you have made

00:34:43.639 --> 00:34:45.639
you run it

00:34:45.639 --> 00:34:47.639
once

